    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# SnackCheck - Nutrition Check\n\n## Purpose\nTurn a product barcode into a friendly health verdict using Open Food Facts data and a short AI-written paragraph.\n\n## How It Works\n1. Webhook receives { \"barcode\": \"...\" }.\n2. Body and barcode are validated.\n3. Open Food Facts is queried (free, no key).\n4. Sugar, salt and fat per 100 g are classified with UK traffic-light thresholds; a concern score (0-3) is computed.\n5. Verdict = worse of traffic-light level and Nutri-Score level.\n6. Anthropic Claude writes a cautionary (unhealthy) or encouraging (healthy/moderate) paragraph.\n7. A formatted plain-text verdict is returned.\n\n## Setup\nOnly an Anthropic API credential is needed (attached to both Anthropic Chat Model nodes). Open Food Facts requires no key. Publish the workflow to enable the production URL.\n\n## Usage\nPOST /webhook/nutrition-check with JSON { \"barcode\": \"3017620422003\" }.\n\n## Error Handling\n- Empty body {}: 200 JSON usage docs\n- Body present but barcode missing, empty, or non-numeric (e.g. {\"foo\":1}, {\"barcode\":\"\"}, {\"barcode\":\"abc\"}): 400 invalid_barcode\n- Barcode not in Open Food Facts: 404 product_not_found\n- Product found but sugar, salt and fat are ALL missing: 200 insufficient_data (even if a Nutri-Score exists, no verdict is given)\n\n## Limitations\nData quality depends on Open Food Facts contributors. Thresholds are per 100 g, not per portion. One barcode per request. AI text is advisory, not medical advice.\n- If Open Food Facts is down or returns a malformed response, the user sees \"product not found\" because the HTTP node is set to never error.\n- A missing individual nutrient (but not all three) is treated as 0 when classifying.",
        "height": 820,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 4
      },
